  "OverallSummary": "This case involves Independent Financial Group, LLC's (IFG) failure to establish and maintain a supervisory system reasonably designed to supervise representatives' 529 plan rollover recommendations from September 2015 to the present. The firm specifically failed to establish policies or procedures regarding available sales charge waivers or special share classes (Class AR) for state-to-state 529 plan rollovers, which would have decreased costs for customers. The violations affected at least 18 customers with total rollover dollars of at least $837,000, resulting in approximately $17,000 in unnecessary sales charges and fees. The violations cited are of MSRB Rule G-27 (failure to supervise) and, after June 30, 2020, Reg BI's Compliance Obligation under Exchange Act Rule 15l-1(a)(1), not the Care Obligation specifically. As part of the settlement, IFG agreed to pay a $75,000 fine and provide restitution plus interest to eligible customers who qualified for but did not receive applicable sales charge waivers or Class AR shares. The firm also agreed to retain a Third-Party Consultant to review its procedures, identify eligible customers, and calculate restitution amounts. The case demonstrates how supervisory failures in providing available fee waivers can lead to customers paying higher costs than necessary for 529 plan rollovers, even when those products themselves may be appropriate investment vehicles for education savings."
